<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Decembrists</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1825</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Decembrist revolt</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Decembrists were Russian army officers and nobles who staged a revolt in St Petersburg on 14 December 1825 (Old Style), refusing to swear allegiance to Nicholas I and seeking a constitution or a republic and the end of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serfdom">serfdom</a>. The rising, and a second in the south, was quickly crushed; five leaders were hanged and over a hundred exiled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siberia">Siberia</a>. Later Russian liberals and revolutionaries honoured them as martyrs.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/decembrists.jpg" alt="Decembrists" width="320" height="209" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vasily Timm · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Georg_Wilhelm_Timm_-_Dekabristen-Aufstand.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
